+
+## Multiple Firefox instances
+
+Every MCP tool accepts an optional non-empty string `id`. The first call using a
+new ID launches a separate Firefox browser; subsequent calls reuse that instance.
+Agents sharing an MCP server should each choose a unique ID and pass it on every
+call, for example:
+
+```json
+{"name":"navigate_page","arguments":{"id":"agent-a","url":"https://example.com"}}
+{"name":"take_snapshot","arguments":{"id":"agent-a"}}
+{"name":"navigate_page","arguments":{"id":"agent-b","url":"https://example.org"}}
+```
+
+Omitting `id` selects the shared `default` instance, as does `"id":"default"`.
+Each instance has its own tabs, selected page, snapshots, console and network
+state. Initialization is shared for simultaneous calls using the same ID, while
+different IDs can launch independently. Closing/disconnecting one browser only
+causes that instance to be relaunched on its next call. IDs are local to the MCP
+server process and are not persistent Firefox profile names.
+
+For `get_network_request`, use `requestId` for the network request identifier
+returned by `list_network_requests`; `id` now selects the browser, just as on all
+other tools:
+
+```json
+{"name":"get_network_request","arguments":{"id":"agent-a","requestId":"request-123"}}
+```
 
